      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "What you are describing sounds like you might be experiencing some unusual sensory perception changes. While it's possible that your brain is adapting to environmental stimuli, seeing thermal signatures and hearing electrical hums in unexpected ways can warrant a conversation with a healthcare professional. They can help determine if this is a normal physiological adaptation or if further investigation is needed. It's always best to get a professional evaluation for concerning sensory experiences.",
